/ The device that separates the two registers on a case page, and labels the
/ sections of the index. On the index the label *is* the section heading, so it
/ renders as an h2 there; above a case-page h2 it stays a plain span.
.wk-track class="wk-track--#{tone}"
  = content_tag(local_assigns.fetch(:heading, :span), label, class: 'wk-track__label')
  span.wk-track__rule
